lso":"Beelzebub","summary":"Adversary; accuser. When used as a proper name, the Hebrew word so rendered has the article “the adversary” (Job 1:6-12; 2:1-7).","verses":55,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[22]},{"id":"portius_2367","name":"Portius","also":"Porcius","summary":"The successor of Felix (A.D. 60) as procurator of Judea (Acts 24:27). A few weeks after he had entered on his office the case of Paul, then a prisoner at Caesarea, was reported to him.","verses":12,"father":"","mother":"","v":[24,25,32]},{"id":"bernice_482","name":"Bernice","also":"","summary":"Bearer of victory, the eldest daughter of Agrippa I., the Herod Agrippa of Acts 12:20. After the early death of her first husband she was married to her uncle Herod, king of Chalcis.","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[30]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[4,10,20]},{"id":"nazareth_878","name":"Nazareth","kind":"City","lat":32.70103,"lon":35.30015,"summary":"Separated, generally supposed to be the Greek form of the Hebrew netser, a “shoot” or “sprout.”","verses":28,"v":[9]},{"id":"damascus_322","name":"Damascus","kind":"City","lat":33.51161,"lon":36.3091,"summary":"Activity, the most ancient of Oriental cities; the capital of Syria (Isa. 7:8; 17:3); situated about 133 miles to the north of Jerusalem.","verses":55,"v":[12,20]},{"id":"judea_657","name":"Judea","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"After the Captivity this name was applied to the whole of the country west of the Jordan (